The author is not aware of any patents that cover the algorithms implemented 
here. The core techniques used are:

Audio:
  - MDCT / IMDCT with sine window (Princen-Bradley, 1986–87; expired)
  - TDAC (Time-Domain Aliasing Cancellation, 1986; expired)
  - Mid/Side stereo coding (Blumlein, 1930s; classic technique)
  - Bark-scale band partitioning (Barkhausen 1960s, public domain)
  - Absolute Threshold of Hearing (Terhardt 1979, public domain)
  - Rice coding (Golomb 1966, Rice 1979; expired)
  - Adaptive per-band quantization (basic idea, expired)

Images:
  - Oklab color space (Björn Ottosson, 2020; public domain)
  - Block DCT (discrete cosine transform; expired)
  - Run-Length Encoding (RLE; public domain)
  - Zstandard compression (Yann Collet, 2015; BSD/GPLv2, patent-free)

